description_html:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Team description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Hardware tribe builds the technology that turns everyday devices into secure, reliable card readers, from Bluetooth-connected dongles to fully in-house Tap to Pay on Android. You&#39;ll join a team solving genuinely hard problems: keeping payments working across flaky Bluetooth connections, handling online and offline flows without losing a transaction. It&#39;s a chance to go deep on Android engineering in a space where reliability really matters, since every merchant depends on these readers to get paid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain Android applications for card readers, SDKs, and the SuperApp, covering both new features and improvements to existing systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work on Bluetooth Low Energy connections, online and offline payment flows, and Tap to Pay functionality&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Refactor and modernise legacy code to improve reliability, performance, and maintainability&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to testing practices, including unit and integration tests, to raise overall code quality&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with peers and stakeholders across the team to manage priorities and shape solutions to technical challenges&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if...&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Several years of professional Android development experience, with solid proficiency in both Java and Kotlin&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong knowledge of clean architecture principles and hands-on experience maintaining Android SDKs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience of writing unit and integration tests, and comfort refactoring legacy code without breaking existing functionality&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines, such as GitHub Actions, and an interest in improving build and release processes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to adapt to ambiguity and shifting priorities, with strong communication skills for working independently with stakeholders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Berlin office. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💶 A corporate pension scheme where we match up to 20% of your contributions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖 Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave plus public holidays and special leave days Numerous other benefits such as Urban Sports Club subsidy, Kita placement assistance, subsidised office lunches&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
